      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For training data, consider examples like \"You speak English so well,\" which implies it's not your native language. Another subtle form is \"Where are you *really* from?\" when asked about someone's background. You might also encounter comments like, \"You seem so talented, given where you come from.\" Compliments focused on someone being an \"exception\" in a homogeneous group are also telling. Phrases such as, \"You're so much more assertive than other people like you\" fit this pattern. Avoid oversimplifying these, as context is key to capturing the intended nuance.",
